# Blade & Quill — Cursor working rules

You are working inside the Blade & Quill Art Academy website project (`artifacts/blade-quill/`). This is Corinne Hadaway's redesign — an art-education site with shop, gallery, downloads, blog, and YouTube-led tutorials.

**Read `BLADE_AND_QUILL.md` in this folder** for brand context, site map, owner notes, and decisions. Prefer that file over chat history when they conflict.

The design system is in active iteration. Nothing is locked. Prefer reversible changes; flag when you're about to make something hard to undo.

---

## Stack

- **Vite + React (TS)**, port 3001
- **Tailwind v4** — uses the new `@theme inline` syntax in `src/index.css`. Do NOT scaffold a `tailwind.config.{js,ts}` file; v4 doesn't use one for theme.
- **shadcn/ui** in the *new-york* style, *neutral* base. Primitives live in `src/components/ui/`. Don't modify those files unless updating to the latest shadcn version — they're regenerable.
- **TinaCMS** for content (running at port 4001 in dev), **Wouter** for routing
- **next-themes** is installed for dark-mode wiring
- Hosted on Replit (Replit Vite plugins are in `vite.config.ts`)

## Design system source of truth

The single source of truth for tokens is the `@theme inline` block + `:root` and `.dark` selectors in `src/index.css`. The foundations doc and `tokens.json` (in the Cowork workspace) are reference materials, not the build input — keep them in sync manually for now.

When asked to add or change a color, type, spacing, or radius value, **edit `src/index.css` directly**. Don't introduce a separate `tailwind.config.ts` or a `theme.ts` file — that fragments the source.

## Color rules

- **Semantic tokens are the default.** Use `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.
- **Brand tokens** (`text-charcoal`, `text-rose`, `text-orange`, `text-amber`, `text-violet`, `bg-cream`) are allowed for explicit, intentional brand moments. Examples: price badges (orange), section dividers (cream), illustration accents (amber).
- **Raw hex values are forbidden** in TSX/JSX. If you need a color that isn't in the system, add it to `index.css` first, then use the new token.
- **Never use Tailwind's default color palette** (`bg-red-500`, `text-blue-600`, etc.). Use semantic or brand tokens.

## Typography rules

- **Body** uses `font-sans` (Quicksand) at `font-light` (300) by default. If text reads too thin, bump to `font-normal` (400) — don't add new weights.
- **Headings** use `font-sans` at `font-medium` (500) or `font-normal` (400), with `tracking-normal` and `leading-tight`. Use the existing pattern in `@layer base h1-h6` rules.
- **Display** (`font-display`, Young Serif) is reserved for `<h1>`. Do not use it for other text.
- Loading new fonts requires updating `index.html`, not adding new `@import` rules in CSS.

## Dark mode

- Dark mode is supported via a `.dark` class on `<html>` or `<body>`. Toggle should write to `localStorage` and respect `prefers-color-scheme` on first load.
- When writing new components, never hardcode colors that wouldn't translate to dark mode. If a component looks different in dark, that's a token issue — fix the token, not the component.
- Use `next-themes` (already installed) for the toggle wiring rather than hand-rolling.

## Components

- Custom B&Q components live in `src/components/blade-quill/` (create the folder when you first add one).
- shadcn primitives live in `src/components/ui/`.
- Layout components live in `src/components/layout/`.
- Page blocks (for landing pages) live in `src/pages/blocks/`.
- Use **`class-variance-authority`** (already installed) for component variants. Don't roll a custom variants helper.
- Use **`clsx` + `cn` from `@/lib/utils`** for conditional classNames. There's an existing `cn` helper — use it.
- Prefer composition over props explosion. A `Card` with `<Card.Header>`, `<Card.Body>`, `<Card.Footer>` beats a `Card` with twelve boolean props.

## Existing utility classes worth knowing about

These live in `src/index.css` under `@layer utilities` and represent real, named patterns:

- `.gumroad-card` — primary product/content card, white surface, 4px hover lift
- `.thumb-card` — lighter grid card, 2px hover lift
- `.tag-pill`, `.tag-pill-active`, `.tag-pill-inactive` — category/filter pills
- `.cta-bold` — primary CTA button treatment
- `.dl-btn` — download button (full-width, scales on click)
- `.hover-overlay` — gallery hover gradient
- `.price-badge` — bold orange price (uses `text-orange` — make sure `--color-orange` is the true orange `#e07b3a`, not rose)
- `.reading-width` — 65ch container for long-form prose

When promoting one of these to a React component, **keep the utility class as a fallback** for content authors using TinaCMS or marketing-page authoring. The React component is the typed version; the utility class is the escape hatch.

## Motion

- House easing curve: `cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94)` — use this for all transitions unless there's a specific reason not to.
- Durations: 150ms (fast), 200ms (base), 300ms (smooth), 350ms (slow), 400ms (slower). Don't introduce new durations without reason.
- Hover lifts: 1–4px translate-Y, paired with a corresponding shadow.

## Accessibility

- Run a contrast check (4.5:1 AA normal, 3:1 AA large) on any new color combination.
- Focus rings use `--ring` (which equals primary). Don't remove focus rings — restyle them.
- All interactive elements need a hover, focus, and active state.
- Buttons, links, and form controls should have a minimum tap target of 44×44px on mobile.

## File naming

- React components: `PascalCase.tsx`
- Hooks: `camelCase.ts` starting with `use`
- Utilities: `kebab-case.ts`
- Pages live in `src/pages/PascalCase.tsx`
- Blocks live in `src/pages/blocks/PascalCaseBlock.tsx`

## When making structural changes

- Don't introduce new tooling (Style Dictionary, Storybook, etc.) without flagging first. The user has said the system is not locked yet — keep changes lightweight and reversible.
- Don't move files between folders without flagging. Imports across the codebase will break.
- Don't add new top-level dependencies without flagging. `package.json` already pulls from a workspace catalog — adding deps requires touching the parent workspace.

## When you're unsure

- Reference `foundations.html` in the parent Cowork workspace for the visual canon.
- Reference `tokens.json` in the parent Cowork workspace for the token reference.
- Ask before locking design decisions. The four open issues (orange, Inter, font choice, dark mode) have been resolved as of 2026-04-26 — the rest of the system is still negotiable.
